ر السابق:\n\n```bash\ncpanm XML::Writer\n```\n\n### الخطوة 3 — اختبار nikto\n\n```bash\ncd ~/nikto\nperl program/nikto.pl -h nmap.org -maxtime 60s -nointeractive 2>&1 | tail -30\n```\n\n**أرسل مخرجات `cpanm XML::Writer` أولاً.** إن نجح التثبيت، سيعمل nikto."}]},{"id":403,"parent_id":402,"role":"USER","status":"FINISHED","thinking_enabled":false,"search_enabled":true,"accumulated_token_usage":286137,"inserted_at":"2026-10-05T00:37:30.160Z","fragments":[{"type":"REQUEST","content":"~/nikto $ pkg install -y cpanminus make clang\ncpanm XML::Writer\nChecking availability of current mirror:\n[*] https://mirrors.ravidwivedi.in/termux/termux-main: ok\nReading package lists... Done\nBuilding dependency tree... Done\nReading state information... Done\nE: Unable to locate package cpanminus\nNo command cpanm found, did you mean:\n Command cpan in package perl\n~/nikto $ pkg install -y perl-xml-writer 2>/dev/null || echo \"trying cpan\"\nChecking availability of current mirror:\n[*] https://mirrors.ravidwivedi.in/termux/termux-main: ok\nReading package lists... Done\nBuilding dependency tree... Done\nReading state information... Done                     trying cpan\n~/nikto $ cpan App::cpanminus\nLoading internal logger. Log::Log4perl recommended for better logging\n\nCPAN.pm requires configuration, but most of it can be done automatically.\nIf you answer 'no' below, you will enter an interactive dialog for each                                     configuration option instead.                         \nWould you like to configure as much as possible automatically? [yes]\n\nTrying with                                               /data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/wget -O \"/data/data/com.termux/files/home/.cpan/sources/authors/01mailrc.txt.gz.tmp28793\"\nto get\n    https://cpan.org/authors/01mailrc.txt.gz\n--2026-10-05 01:34:33--  https://cpan.org/authors/01mailrc.txt.gz                                           Resolving cpan.org (cpan.org)... 151.101.1.55, 151.101.193.55, 1